9. Conclusion
The experiment demonstrates that hashCode() and equals() must follow the Java contract when using HashSet.

Overriding equals() alone is not sufficient because HashSet uses hashCode() to locate the correct bucket before comparing objects.

By overriding hashCode() using the registration number, duplicate attendance records can be prevented.

HashSet is suitable for fast attendance de-duplication, TreeSet is useful when sorted attendance records are required, and HashMap is useful when registration numbers must be mapped to student details.

Therefore, HashSet with correctly overridden equals() and hashCode() is my recommended solution for the college fest attendance system.
